WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Nosebleeds are very common and, in most cases, they are not serious.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.960
Our main goals are simply to stop the bleeding and make sure the person doesn't swallow

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.360
any blood.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.720
To start, have the person sit down and lean forward.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.760
Be sure they do not tilt their head back, as that can cause blood to run down their

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.760
throat.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.760
Next, you'll want to firmly pinch the soft lower part of the nose, right at the nostrils,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.879
and hold that continuous pressure for at least 10 to 15 minutes.

00:00:27.879 --> 00:00:31.360
It's important not to release the pressure to check on it too early, and you should

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.520
avoid packing the nose with cotton or tissues.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.240
If the bleeding doesn't stop after that initial pressure, you can try applying an

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.680
ice pack to the bridge of the nose while continuing to pinch the nostrils.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.480
While we can usually handle these ourselves, you should seek medical care if you think

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.240
the nose might be broken.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.119
Go ahead and call 911 if the bleeding hasn't stopped after 15 minutes, or if the person

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.560
is having trouble breathing.

